              Awaiting operator input.
            </p>
          </aside>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-share-bar">
          <div>
            <span>Field note / 001</span>
            <strong
              >“The model is rarely the bottleneck. The company is.”</strong
            >
          </div>
          <a href={X_SHARE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Post this on X <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="proof-ribbon" aria-label="Career proof points">
        <div>
          <strong>10+</strong>
          <span>years in engineering</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <strong>8</strong>
          <span>years as CTO + founder</span>
        </div>
        <a href={FORBES_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <strong>Forbes</strong>
          <span>OdeCloud profile ↗</span>
        </a>
        <div>
          <strong>Enterprise</strong>
          <span>JVC Kenwood · Coinbase · WarnerMedia</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="offer-chapter" aria-labelledby="offer-heading">
        <div class="offer-heading" data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow">Three ways in</p>
          <h2 id="offer-heading">Choose your next move.</h2>
          <p>
            Bring me the hard decision, read the field manual, or get the next
            useful idea in your inbox.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="offer-grid">
          <article id="consulting" data-reveal="right">
            <div class="offer-index">
              <span>01 / Decision session</span>
              <i>60 minutes</i>
            </div>
            <h3>One consequential decision. One clear next move.</h3>
            <p>
              Bring the AI bet, architecture question, product tradeoff, or team
              problem that cannot survive another meeting.
            </p>
            <div class="offer-price">
              <strong>From $300</strong>
              <span>Projects + retainers scoped separately</span>
            </div>
            <a href={LINKEDIN_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Request a session <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </article>

          <article data-reveal="up">
            <div class="offer-index">
              <span>02 / The book</span>
              <i>Read now</i>
            </div>
            <h3>Lead engineering without becoming the hero.</h3>
            <p>
              Read <cite>Emperors, Prophets, and Product Managers</cite>—my
              field guide to engineering leadership, management, and recurring
              organizational chaos.
            </p>
            <a href={AMAZON_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
              Get the book <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </article>

          <article class="offer-newsletter" data-reveal="left">
            <div class="offer-index">
              <span>03 / Field notes</span>
              <i>Free</i>
            </div>
            <h3>Get the playbook as I learn it.</h3>
            <p>
              Practical AI tips, industry shortcuts, getting hired, and candid
              dispatches from building a company across cultures.
            </p>
            <a href="#newsletter" data-focus-newsletter>
              Join the newsletter <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        class="work-chapter"
        id="work"
        data-chapter="work"
        aria-labelledby="work-heading"
      >
        <div class="chapter-register chapter-register-dark" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Act 01 / Experience</span>
          <span>Code · company · people</span>
        </div>

        <div class="work-layout">
          <div class="work-heading" data-reveal="left">
            <p class="eyebrow">The operating range</p>
            <h2 id="work-heading">From the codebase to the boardroom.</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="work-story" data-reveal="right">
            <p class="lead">
              I started as the engineer who could work anywhere in the stack.
              Over 10+ years, the scope expanded: product, hiring, strategy,
              leadership—and now agentic AI.
            </p>
            <p>
              At OdeCloud, I’ve spent eight years as CTO and founder,
              translating what the business needs into systems teams can
              actually build, operate, and grow.
            </p>
            <div class="advisory-callout">
              <span>The throughline</span>
              <p>
                Make complex technology legible. Give technical teams enough
                context to make good decisions—and business leaders enough
                clarity to trust them.
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="enterprise-proof">
              OdeCloud has delivered work for enterprise teams including JVC
              Kenwood, Coinbase, and WarnerMedia.
              <a href={FORBES_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                Read the OdeCloud Forbes profile ↗
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="expertise-card" data-reveal="up">
            <p>Experience / current</p>
            <ul>{expertise.map(item => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        class="book-chapter"
        id="book"
        data-chapter="book"
        aria-labelledby="book-heading"
      >
        <div class="chapter-register" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Act 02 / The book</span>
          <span>Prophet’s guides — field manual № 001</span>
        </div>

        <div class="book-layout">
          <figure class="book-stage" data-reveal="left">
            <div class="book-shadow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="book-frame">
              <img
                src="assets/book-cover.jpg?v=3"
                width="1600"
                height="2560"
                alt="Cover of Emperors, Prophets, and Product Managers by Vanielle Lee"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <figcaption>Cover artwork · final edition</figcaption>
          </figure>

          <div class="book-copy" data-reveal="right">
            <p class="eyebrow">The new book</p>
            <h2 id="book-heading">
              Leadership has always been chaos.
              <em>The tools just changed.</em>
            </h2>
            <p class="book-lede">
              <cite>Emperors, Prophets, and Product Managers</cite> is a CTO’s
              guide to the patterns that keep resurfacing wherever power,
              prediction, technology, and human judgment meet.
            </p>
            <div class="book-stats" aria-label="Book details">
              <span><strong>12</strong> chapters</span>
              <span><strong>6</strong> frameworks</span>
              <span><strong>1</strong> honest field guide</span>
            </div>
            <a
              class="button button-book"
              href={AMAZON_URL}
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener noreferrer"
            >
              Get the book <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section
        class="notes-chapter"
        id="notes"
        data-chapter="notes"
        aria-labelledby="notes-heading"
      >
        <div class="notes-heading" data-reveal="up">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Act 03 / Field notes</p>
          <h2 id="notes-heading">
            Ideas you can use—even if you don’t write code.
          </h2>
          <p>
            I explain what technology means for the people funding it, building
            it, and living with the outcome.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="dispatch-list">
          <article data-reveal="left">
            <span>01</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Practical AI, without the theater</h3>
              <p>
                What agentic systems can do, where they fail, and what it takes
                to ship them.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article data-reveal="right">
            <span>02</span>
            <div>
              <h3>The unspoken career playbook</h3>
              <p>
                Industry shortcuts, getting hired, and the choices that create
                real career leverage.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article data-reveal="left">
            <span>03</span>
            <div>
              <h3>Cross-cultural founder notes</h3>
              <p>
                Candid lessons from building and leading a company across
                countries, expectations, and working styles.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <a class="notes-cta" href="#newsletter" data-focus-newsletter>
          <span>Open the channel</span>
          <strong>Send me the next field note</strong>
          <i aria-hidden="true">↗</i>
        </a>
      </section>

      <section
        class="connect-chapter"
        id="connect"
        data-chapter="connect"
        aria-labelledby="connect-heading"
      >
        <div data-reveal="left">
          <p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">End credits / Let’s talk</p>
          <h2 id="connect-heading">Bring me the hard decision.</h2>
          <p class="connect-lede">
            Decision sessions start at $300. Projects, speaking, and ongoing
            advisory engagements are scoped separately. Start with a message on
            LinkedIn.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="link-grid" data-reveal="right">
          {
            links.map((link, index) => (
              <a href={link.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                <small>{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</small>
                <span>
                  <strong>{link.label}</strong>
                  <i>{link.handle}</i>
                </span>
                <b aria-hidden="true">↗</b>
              </a>
            ))
          }
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
      <p>AI engineer · Founder · CTO</p>
      <a href="#newsletter" data-focus-newsletter>Join the field notes ↑</a>
      <p>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Vanielle Lee</p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const shell = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".site-shell");

  if (shell && shell.dataset.motionReady !== "true") {
    shell.dataset.motionReady = "true";
    const reduceMotion = window.matchMedia(
      "(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)"
    ).matches;

    if (!reduceMotion) {
      shell.classList.add("motion-ready");
      const reveals = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-reveal]");
      const revealObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
        entries => {
          entries.forEach(entry => {
            if (entry.isIntersecting) {
              entry.target.classList.add("is-visible");
              revealObserver.unobserve(entry.target);
            }
          });
        },
        { threshold: 0.08, rootMargin: "0px 0px -12% 0px" }
      );
      reveals.forEach(element => revealObserver.observe(element));
    }

    const chapterLinks = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>(
      "[data-chapter-link]"
    );
    const chapters = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-chapter]");
    const chapterObserver = new IntersectionObserver(
      entries => {
        const current = entries
          .filter(entry => entry.isIntersecting)
          .sort((a, b) => b.intersectionRatio - a.intersectionRatio)[0];
        if (!current) return;

        const chapter =
          current.target instanceof HTMLElement
            ? current.target.dataset.chapter
            : undefined;
        chapterLinks.forEach(link => {
          if (link.dataset.chapterLink === chapter) {
            link.setAttribute("aria-current", "location");
          } else {
            link.removeAttribute("aria-current");
          }
        });
      },
      { threshold: 0.01, rootMargin: "-45% 0px -45% 0px" }
    );
    chapters.forEach(chapter => chapterObserver.observe(chapter));

    let progressFrame = 0;
    const revealVisible = () => {
      if (reduceMotion) return;
      document
        .querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-reveal]")
        .forEach(element => {
          const bounds = element.getBoundingClientRect();
          if (bounds.top < window.innerHeight * 0.88 && bounds.bottom > 0) {
            element.classList.add("is-visible");
          }
        });
    };
    const updateProgress = () => {
      const max = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - window.innerHeight;
      const ratio = max > 0 ? window.scrollY / max : 0;
      shell.style.setProperty("--scroll-progress", `${ratio * 100}%`);
      revealVisible();
      progressFrame = 0;
    };
    window.addEventListener(
      "scroll",
      () => {
        if (!progressFrame) {
          progressFrame = window.requestAnimationFrame(updateProgress);
        }
      },
      { passive: true }
    );
    updateProgress();

    document
      .querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>("[data-focus-newsletter]")
      .forEach(link => {
        link.addEventListener("click", () => {
          window.setTimeout(
            () => {
              document
                .querySelector<HTMLInputElement>("#newsletter-email")
                ?.focus({ preventScroll: true });
            },
            reduceMotion ? 0 : 650
          );
        });
      });

    const diagnosticTrigger = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>(
      "[data-run-diagnostic]"
    );
    const diagnosticResult = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>(
      "[data-diagnostic-result]"
    );
    const diagnosticRows = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(
      "[data-diagnostic-row]"
    );

    diagnosticTrigger?.addEventListener("click", () => {
      diagnosticTrigger.disabled = true;
      diagnosticTrigger.classList.add("is-running");
      diagnosticTrigger.innerHTML =
        'Scanning the organization <span aria-hidden="true">•••</span>';
      if (diagnosticResult) diagnosticResult.textContent = "Scanning…";

      diagnosticRows.forEach((row, index) => {
        row.classList.remove("is-scanned");
        const status = row.querySelector<HTMLElement>("i");
        if (status) status.textContent = "SCANNING";

        window.setTimeout(
          () => {
            row.style.setProperty(
              "--diagnostic-score",
              `${row.dataset.score}%`
            );
            row.classList.add("is-scanned");
            if (status) status.textContent = row.dataset.result ?? "CHECKED";
          },
          reduceMotion ? 0 : 220 + index * 260
        );
      });

      window.setTimeout(
        () => {
          diagnosticTrigger.disabled = false;
          diagnosticTrigger.classList.remove("is-running");
          diagnosticTrigger.innerHTML =
            'Run it again <span aria-hidden="true">↻</span>';
          if (diagnosticResult) {
            diagnosticResult.textContent =
              "Finding: the model was not the bottleneck.";
          }
        },
        reduceMotion ? 30 : 1750
      );
    });
  }
</script>

<style>
  :global(html) {
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    scroll-padding-top: 5rem;
  }
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #11110f;
    color: #191915;
    font-family: "Instrument Sans", Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;
  }
  :global(*) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  .site-shell {
    --ink: #171713;
    --ink-soft: #24231f;
    --paper: #f1ecdf;
    --paper-bright: #fbf8ef;
    --red: #cf2f21;
    --red-bright: #e63b2c;
    --amber: #d9a738;
    --salmon: #ef746d;
    --muted: #777064;
    --scroll-progress: 0%;
    min-height: 100vh;
    overflow: clip;
    background: var(--ink);
  }
  .site-shell > main {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .site-shell main > section,
  .site-shell > footer {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: none;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .opening-sequence {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    pointer-events: none;
    animation: sequence-exit 1ms linear 1.72s forwards;
  }
  .shutter {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 51%;
    background: linear-gradient(rgba(25, 25, 21, 0.045) 1px, transparent 1px),
      var(--paper);
    background-size: 100% 30px;
  }
  .shutter::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 2rem;
    bottom: 2rem;
    width: 1px;
    background: var(--ink);
  }
  .shutter-left {
    left: 0;
    animation: shutter-left 900ms cubic-bezier(0.78, 0, 0.2, 1) 0.72s forwards;
  }
  .shutter-left::after {
    right: 2rem;
  }
  .shutter-right {
    right: 0;
    animation: shutter-right 900ms cubic-bezier(0.78, 0, 0.2, 1) 0.72s forwards;
  }
  .shutter-right::after {
    left: 2rem;
  }
  .opening-slate {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    width: min(540px, calc(100% - 3rem));
    padding: 1.4rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.55rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    background: var(--paper-bright);
    color: var(--ink);
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    text-align: center;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    animation: slate-out 380ms ease 0.62s forwards;
  }
  .opening-slate span,
  .opening-slate i {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.63rem;
    font-style: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  }
  .opening-slate strong {
    color: var(--red);
    font-family: "Bodoni Moda", Didot, serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .scroll-progress {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: 80;
    height: 3px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.13);
  }
  .scroll-progress-fill {
    width: var(--scroll-progress);
    height: 100%;
    display: block;
    background: var(--red-bright);
    transition: width 70ms linear;
  }

  .mission-nav {
    position: fixed;
    top: 3px;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    z-index: 70;
